@startuml persona-layout
title On-disk persona layout

skinparam backgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam defaultFontColor #333333
skinparam folderBackgroundColor #ecfccb
skinparam folderBorderColor #d1d5db
skinparam fileBackgroundColor #fef3c7
skinparam fileBorderColor #d1d5db
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam packageBorderColor #d1d5db
skinparam arrowColor #2563eb
skinparam noteBorderColor #d1d5db
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #f9fafb

folder "<octowright-config>/profiles/" as ROOT {
  folder "dante/" as DANTE {
    file "profile.yaml\n  display_name, default_url,\n  default_macros, credentials, app" as DY
    file "avatar.png\n(arbitrary persona files;\noctowright ignores)" as DA
    folder "webkit/\nPlaywright user-data-dir" as DW
    folder "chromium/\nPlaywright user-data-dir" as DC
    folder "firefox/\nPlaywright user-data-dir" as DF
  }

  folder "tim/" as TIM {
    file "profile.yaml" as TY
    folder "webkit/" as TW
  }
}

note right of DANTE
  A **persona** is the top-level identity.
  It owns metadata + arbitrary sidecar files.
end note

note right of DY
  `default_url` is also the context's
  Playwright **base_url**, so a macro can
  navigate `/orders` rather than an origin.
  The macro is the BEHAVIOUR; the persona
  is the WHERE — swap persona to replay the
  same macro against another deployment.
end note

note right of DW
  An **engine profile** is `<persona>/<kind>/`.
  This is what Playwright's `user_data_dir`
  points at when `browser_launch(profile=dante, kind=webkit)`.
  Browser writes only here; octowright never touches it.
end note

@enduml
